# SecuBox Profiles — the /profiles/ panel (User=secubox) delegates apply/rollback
# to the root helper secubox-profilectl (webui→ctl pattern, see
# .claude/MODULE-COMPLIANCE.md → Privileged Operations).
#
# The CLI is launched via `systemd-run`, NOT plain sudo: this service runs under
# ProtectSystem=strict with a reduced ReadWritePaths, and a `sudo` child inherits
# that mount namespace — the CLI would see the snapshot dir, audit log, WAF routes
# and /data/lxc as READ-ONLY (EROFS) and could not drive systemd/LXC. A transient
# `systemd-run` unit runs in PID 1's context, OUTSIDE the sandbox, with the access
# the actuator needs.
#
# Exact-command grants (no wildcards, no flag escapes) — the panel always builds
# this FIXED argv (--only stays a root-CLI-only affordance):
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-profilectl apply --yes --json
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-profilectl rollback --yes --json

# secubox-waker (User=secubox, ProtectSystem=strict) — same webui->ctl +
# systemd-run pattern for its own privileged operation: waking a single
# on-demand module (api/waker.py::_fire_wake). Fire-and-forget (no --wait/
# --pipe: the waker never blocks an HTTP request on the wake's outcome,
# unlike the panel's apply/rollback above which DOES wait for the result).
#
# The trailing `*` is a deliberate, bounded exception to the "no wildcards"
# rule above: the module id is a genuine per-call variable (one wake per
# vhost), so it cannot be a fixed string like apply/rollback's argv. This is
# still safe because:
#   - sudo never invokes a shell here — the matched argv is executed
#     directly (execve), so shell metacharacters in the glob match (;, |,
#     $(), ..) are inert, they are just literal bytes in one argv element;
#   - secubox-wakectl's own argparse treats `module` as a single positional
#     value, never re-parsed as flags or re-shelled;
#   - secubox-wakectl further validates that value against load_all() and
#     REFUSES anything that isn't a known module id (status="refused",
#     reason="unknown") before it drives systemd/LXC.
# So the wildcard only ever resolves to "a manifest id known to this system,
# plus --json" — never to arbitrary code execution or an arbitrary argv.
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-wakectl wake *

# Task 10 (#896) — manual sleep/wake buttons on the /profiles/ panel itself
# (api/web.py POST /wake, POST /sleep). Two MORE grants, distinct from both
# sections above:
#
#   * /wake — same secubox-wakectl binary as the waker's fire-and-forget
#     grant just above, but SYNCHRONOUS (--wait --pipe): the panel waits for
#     and displays the wake report to the operator, unlike the waker (which
#     never blocks a public, unauthenticated HTTP request on the wake's
#     outcome). The extra --wait --pipe flags make this a DIFFERENT command
#     line that does not match the fire-and-forget grant above, hence its
#     own line here. Same wildcard-safety argument as above applies
#     verbatim: execve (no shell) + secubox-wakectl re-validates the module
#     id itself (refuses unknown/manual/always-on before touching
#     systemd/LXC).
#
#   * /sleep — reuses the EXISTING `apply` actuator (no new binary, no new
#     privileged code path), restricted to one module via `--only <id>`:
#     plan_changes already computes a STOP for any sleepable module that is
#     currently up and not desired ON (absent from the active profile /
#     not pinned on), so `--only` simply narrows apply's effect to that one
#     module — if the module IS desired ON, the filtered plan is empty
#     (safe no-op). The wildcard is bounded the same way as the two grants
#     above: sudo matches argv directly (execve, no shell), and
#     secubox-profilectl's own plan_changes only ever acts on a module id it
#     recognizes from modules.d — an unknown id just filters the plan down
#     to nothing, never arbitrary execution.
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-wakectl wake *
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-profilectl apply --only * --yes --json

# Lifecycle setter (#896) — the /profiles/ panel's per-module "awake level"
# selector (api/web.py POST /lifecycle) writes the module manifest
# (/etc/secubox/modules.d/<id>.toml, root:root) and resyncs the derived files,
# so it too delegates to the root ctl via systemd-run. THREE wildcards (module,
# lifecycle value, wake_class value), each a genuine per-call variable — bounded
# exactly like the grants above:
#   - sudo executes the matched argv directly (execve, no shell): metacharacters
#     in any wildcard match are inert literal bytes in one argv element;
#   - the panel pre-validates ALL THREE against CLOSED sets before building this
#     fixed argv — lifecycle ∈ LIFECYCLES, wake_class ∈ WAKE_CLASSES (422), and
#     module ∈ load_all() (404) — so it never emits an out-of-set value;
#   - secubox-profilectl re-validates independently: argparse `choices=` rejects
#     any non-enum lifecycle/wake_class (exit before any write), and set-lifecycle
#     refuses a module id absent from modules.d (status=refused) before writing.
# So the wildcards only ever resolve to "a known module id + two enum values +
# --json" — never arbitrary code or an arbitrary argv.
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-profilectl set-lifecycle * --lifecycle * --wake-class * --json

# Reveil d'une application Streamlit (#1018). Verbe SEPARE de `wake` : le
# grant existant vise le prefixe litteral « wake », qui ne couvre pas
# « wake-streamlit » — ajouter le second n'elargit donc pas le premier.
#
# Le reveilleur ne pilote jamais le conteneur lui-meme : il tire ce ctl, qui
# demarre l'unite streamlit-app@<appli>. Le nom d'application est valide par
# une liste blanche stricte cote ctl AVANT d'entrer dans un nom d'unite.
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-wakectl wake-streamlit *
